  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The average (arithmetic mean) age of a group consisting of doctors and lawyers is \\(40.\\) If the doctors average \\(35\\) and the lawyers \\(50\\) years old, then the ratio of the number of doctors to the number of lawyers is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(3:2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(3:1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2:3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2:1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(1:2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": "2:1"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1973-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If there are \\(d\\) doctors and \\(\\ell\\) lawyers, then \\[ 35d+50\\ell=40(d+\\ell). \\] Thus \\(5d=10\\ell,\\) so \\[ d:\\ell=2:1. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(d\\) and \\(\\ell\\) be the numbers of doctors and lawyers",
        "Equate the total age \\(35d+50\\ell\\) to \\(40(d+\\ell)\\)"
      ],
